  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A no-pick 2D chamfer now reads a drafted side as a wall. It does not read it as a modelled chamfer.\n- The chamfer takes a third section of the material, half way between the top plane and the corner plane.\n- A piece of a top loop is a drafted wall when two conditions are true:\n  - It stands off the wall by no more than `depth * tan(15 deg)`.\n  - The half-depth section stands half that distance off the wall (within a quarter). The face is one straight face.\n- A loop with drafted pieces and no bevelled piece rides its wall at the corner depth. It counts with the sharp loops (#2596). Thus a plate with no modelled chamfer breaks every edge, the drafted side and the pocket included.\n- `partly_bevelled` becomes `read`, which returns a `Reading`. The #2887 refusal text does not change.\n- `ride_loops` takes two new arguments: `mid` (the half-depth section) and `depth`. The one caller, `material_source.rs`, makes the half-depth section.\n\n## Cause\n\nPR #2894 refuses a loop that is bevelled on only part of its length. It reads each piece more than 0.05 mm off the wall as \"bevelled\". A drafted side also stands off the wall. With a 1 mm chamfer and a 90 degree cone, a draft of more than about 3 degrees is more than 0.05 mm off. The plate was refused with a \"modelled chamfer\" message.\n\nTwo sections cannot tell a draft from a small modelled chamfer. A third section can: a draft is straight, so the half-depth section is at half the offset. A modelled chamfer that ends above half depth puts that section on the vertical wall.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/chamfer_ride_tests.rs`:\n\n- `a_plate_with_one_drafted_side_rides_its_wall`: #2887's plate with its X0 side drafted 3.5, 5 and 10 degrees. Red on unchanged code: `the edge loop near X0.087 Y20.000 carries a modelled chamfer on only part of its length`.\n- `a_small_bevel_on_one_side_is_no_draft`: a 0.2 mm modelled bevel on one side is still refused.\n- `a_straight_face_steeper_than_a_draft_is_a_chamfer`: a 45 degree bevel deeper than the ride is still refused.\n- The #2887 tests (`a_loop_bevelled_on_one_side_refuses_by_name`, `..._with_an_extra_vertex_too`) still pass. The old test calls go through a small `ride` helper.\n\nMutation checks (each guard taken out, then put back):\n\n- Drafted reading off: `a_plate_with_one_drafted_side_rides_its_wall` red.\n- Half-depth check off: `a_small_bevel_on_one_side_is_no_draft` red.\n- Slope limit off: `a_straight_face_steeper_than_a_draft_is_a_chamfer` red.\n- Drafted match arm after the vertex-gap arm: the 3.5 degree case of the drafted pin red (it rode the top loop, inside the part).\n\nGate:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 139 steps, 0 failed (includes `chamfer_partly_bevelled` and `chamfer_modelled_edge`). Run with `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`: the compile cache did not answer on this machine.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No app-level test with a real drafted STEP or STL model. The pins use hand-built sections.\n- A drafted side under a tilted frame. The check measures along the frame's lean, but no test covers it.\n- Heavy lanes were not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPRs #3058, #2836 and #2714 touch `crates/app/src/operation/material_source.rs`. They change other match arms, not the `Chamfer2D` arm. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2929-chamfer-drafted-side.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: A 2D Chamfer with no picked edges no longer refuses a part with a drafted side as a partly bevelled edge loop; the drafted side is chamfered along its wall.\n\nFixes #2929\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
